  "exec_summary": "The European Commission has published a Delegated Regulation in the Official Journal regarding firms' order execution policies under MiFID II, which will impact financial institutions' compliance obligations. In Belgium and the broader EU, this development is significant as it clarifies expectations for best execution practices. The ECB has also announced plans to extend the use of climate factors in the Eurosystem collateral framework to non-financial corporate credit claims, reflecting the regulator's increasing focus on environmental risk. Meanwhile, Deutsche Bank's headquarters were raided in Frankfurt as part of a probe into its retail banking arm, highlighting the ongoing scrutiny of major financial institutions by European regulators.",
